---
import TutorialLayout from '../../../layouts/TutorialLayout.astro';
import NotebookViewer from '../../../components/tutorials/NotebookViewer.astro';
import { loadNotebook } from '../../../lib/notebook';

const { cells } = loadNotebook('src/data/notebooks/3_casadi_perch.ipynb');

const colabUrl =
  'https://colab.research.google.com/github/CogniPilot/rumoca/blob/main/examples/workflows/3_casadi_perch/perch_nmpc.ipynb';
const githubUrl =
  'https://github.com/CogniPilot/rumoca/tree/main/examples/workflows/3_casadi_perch';
---

<TutorialLayout
  title="Nonlinear MPC with CasADi"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { label: 'Tutorials', href: '/tutorials' },
    { label: 'Code Generation Workflows', href: '/tutorials/workflows' },
    { label: 'Nonlinear MPC with CasADi' },
  ]}
  prev={{ label: 'Symbolic Linearization', href: '/tutorials/workflows/sympy-linearize' }}
  next={{ label: 'On-Manifold EKF', href: '/tutorials/workflows/symforce-ekf' }}
>
  <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
    Rumoca emits the Modelica dynamics as a CasADi expression graph. From there it is one short
    step to a nonlinear MPC: write the cost and constraints, hand the whole problem to IPOPT,
    and let CasADi's algorithmic differentiation supply the Jacobians and Hessians the solver needs.
  </p>

  <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-6">
    The example flies a fixed-wing aircraft through an aggressive perched-landing maneuver &mdash;
    a flight regime where linear controllers based on a hover trim simply do not apply.
  </p>

  <NotebookViewer cells={cells} colabUrl={colabUrl} githubUrl={githubUrl} />
</TutorialLayout>
